Register NVIDIA Nemotron-Labs Dory1.0 (model_type "dory") as a CUDA family of tensorfold-native.

What: a lane backend, zig/src/families/nemotron/dory_native.zig (copied in from the recipe's engine/ at build time, with
its libdory binding dory_api.zig), joins the CUDA registry; `zig build dory -Dnvcc=NVCC -Ddory-src=DIR` builds libdory.so
(the forward pass, engine/*.cu) beside the server. Families with an Options.lanes field get --parallel (libdory keeps one
sequence a stream); a family's snap_lookahead sets the prompt cache's lookahead (Dory keys a state at its own row).
Why: the native engine has no backend for Dory's looped nGPT architecture (input/recurrent/output groups, slerp
residuals, sliding + full attention with head dimension 256, NVFP4 W4A16).
Verified: libdory's logits against an fp32 PyTorch reference (tests/compare.py, tests/compare_long.py: top-1 99-100%,
row invariance across streams), and the served model's chat, thinking, tool calls and prompt cache.
